.TH tkutlfmt n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkutlfmt
.PP
Per\-column display formatting for a \fBtablelist\fR widget, via tablelist's \fB\-formatcommand\fR. The underlying cell value stays unchanged, so sorting and filtering still operate on the raw number while the user sees a grouped / currency / percent / date string. Pairs with \fBtkutils::tkutlsort\fR. Library\-neutral.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tkutils::tkutlfmt 0.1
.CE
.PP
Requires \fBTk\fR and \fBtablelist\fR. Uses \fBtclutils::tunum\fR to parse raw values when present (falls back to a built\-in parser).
.SS Commands
.CS
::tkutils::tkutlfmt::column  tbl col type ?options?
::tkutils::tkutlfmt::columns tbl {col type ?{options}? ...}
.CE
.SS "Format types"
.TS
l l.
type	example (raw → shown)
\fBinteger\fR	\fB1234567\fR → \fB1.234.567\fR
\fBnumber\fR	\fB1234.5\fR  → \fB1.234,50\fR
\fBcurrency\fR	\fB1234.5\fR  → \fB1.234,50 €\fR
\fBpercent\fR	\fB0.125\fR   → \fB12,5 %\fR
\fBdate\fR	\fB1717200000\fR → \fB01.06.2024\fR
.TE
.PP
Numeric types are right\-aligned automatically (override with \fB\-align\fR).
.SS Options
.TS
l l l l.
Option	Default	Applies to	Meaning
\fB\-locale\fR	\fBeu\fR	numeric	\fBeu\fR (\fB.\fR/\fB,\fR) or \fBus\fR (\fB,\fR/\fB.\fR)
\fB\-decimals\fR	type	number/currency/%	decimal places
\fB\-group\fR	locale	numeric	thousands separator
\fB\-decimal\fR	locale	numeric	decimal separator
\fB\-symbol\fR	\fB€\fR	currency	currency symbol
\fB\-symbolpos\fR	\fBpost\fR	currency	\fBpre\fR or \fBpost\fR
\fB\-align\fR	auto	all	\fBright\fR/\fBleft\fR/\fBcenter\fR
\fB\-informat\fR	\fB{}\fR	date	\fBclock scan\fR format (else auto/epoch)
\fB\-outformat\fR	\fB%Y\-%m\-%d\fR	date	\fBclock format\fR format
.TE
.SS Usage
.CS
package require Tk
package require tablelist
package require tkutils::tkutlfmt

tablelist::tablelist .t -columns {0 Article left 0 Price right 0 Share right 0 Date left}
# raw values: Price=1234.5  Share=0.125  Date=epoch
\&.t insert end [list Apple 1234.5 0.125 1717200000]

::tkutils::tkutlfmt::column .t 1 currency
::tkutils::tkutlfmt::column .t 2 percent
::tkutils::tkutlfmt::column .t 3 date -outformat "%d.%m.%Y"
.CE
.PP
Bulk form (optional brace\-grouped options per column):
.CS
::tkutils::tkutlfmt::columns .t {
    1 currency {-symbol $ -symbolpos pre -locale us}
    2 percent
    3 date {-outformat %d.%m.%Y}
}
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Store \fBraw numbers\fR in the cells (e.g. \fB1234.5\fR, not \fB"1.234,50 €"\fR); the formatter renders them and \fBtkutlsort\fR/native sort compares them numerically.
.IP \(bu
Non\-numeric / non\-date cells are passed through unchanged.
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TKUTILS TKUTLFMT <REASON>}\fR (\fBTYPE\fR, \fBOPTION\fR, \fBLOCALE\fR).
